#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101583} :activity/id #uuid "e216932a-7285-534e-b666-8b8934782d02" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050821 :topic/id #uuid "694fcacb-2468-51b2-bf00-fd3c25bc6cba" :topic/math-academy-id 1210} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101583 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101997 :tutorial/content "The function $f(x)$ is differentiable on an open interval containing $x=2$. The values of $f$ and $f'$ are given in the following table:\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $f'(x)$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $2$ | $0$ | $4$ |\n\nLet's find\n\n$$\n\\lim\\limits_{x \\to 2} \\dfrac{f(x)}{x^3-8}\n$$\n\nNotice that if we try to substitute $x=2$ directly into the limit, we reach the indeterminate form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{0}{0}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nlim_(x → 2)(f(x))/(x^{3} - 8) &= \\left.(f(x))/(x^{3} - 8)\\right|_{x = 2} \\\\\n&= (f(2))/(2^{3} - 8) \\\\\n&= \\frac{0}{8 - 8} \\\\\n&= \\frac{0}{0}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we use L'Hopital's rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nlim_(x → 2)(f(x))/(x^{3} - 8) &= lim_(x → 2)((f(x))^{′})/((x^{3} - 8)^{′}) \\\\\n&= lim_(x → 2)(f^{′}(x))/(3x^{2})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute $x=2$ again, and this time, we are able to determine the result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nlim_(x → 2)(f^{′}(x))/(3x^{2}) &= \\left.(f^{′}(x))/(3x^{2})\\right|_{x = 2} \\\\\n&= (f^{′}(2))/(3 \\cdot 2^{2}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{4}{3 \\cdot 2^{2} - 0} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\lim\\limits_{x \\to 2} \\dfrac{f(x)}{x^3-8}=\\dfrac{1}{3}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "c8d2f073-f126-5950-9555-61f8a6dd159a" :tutorial/math-academy-id 599 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "e4ea661d-9e67-59ef-ae74-3ef55f82ab3a" :step/math-academy-id 1137 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101584}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101584 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100811 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100623 :question/id #uuid "127247a2-3209-51aa-acb1-eceeaa0dec33" :question/math-academy-id "e-304"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c185115e-e3ce-5503-ab5f-a3d0b1a49cfd" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050961} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051036}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101223} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101224}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Limit of a Function Given as a Table of Values Using L'Hopital's Rule"} :step/id #uuid "06be6b30-b825-5dbe-9087-f089e5a3c396" :step/math-academy-id 1138 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101585}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101585 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100812 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100624 :question/id #uuid "89a99552-00c5-5850-a567-1b338ab5e16b" :question/math-academy-id "e-305"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "98e43a1e-2073-593b-9b55-4f9c25c356a8" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101225} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101226} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234323}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Limit of a Function Given as a Table of Values Using L'Hopital's Rule Twice"} :step/id #uuid "97a0a8f1-3fcd-5681-9176-f997a3d0c81b" :step/math-academy-id 1142}] :activity/title "L'Hopital's Rule Applied to Tables" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186101065}]}
